course: dictionary
lesson: 3997
title: Many meanings of game
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word game is a good example. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning is right. «We won the game 3–1» means one match, because of the score. It does not mean a toy.
explain: «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now, and the giant pickaxe has gone.» The pickaxe is a clue. It comes from a game on a screen, so games here means video games. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: Game can also be an adjective. «She was game to try the climbing wall» means she was willing to try it. Sometimes the clue is a word like to: game to try, game for a swim. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A game is something you play for fun with rules, like tag, chess or football.
fact: A game can also mean one match: «We won the game 3–1».
fact: «Games» can mean a big sports event, like the Olympic Games.
fact: To be game means to be willing to try something.
fact: In maths, games played = games won + games lost, and points per game is a rate.
exercise: «We won the game 3–1.» What does game mean here? | A toy you hold in your hand | *One match | Wild animals hunted for food
exercise: Sam's team played 10 games and won 6 of them. How many games did they lose? | *4 | 6 | 16 | 3
exercise: Dani says, «I'm game for a swim!» What does game mean? | *Willing to try | A big sports event | A wild animal
test: «Zara swapped the gift card for a game she could use.» What is a game in this sentence? | A wild animal hunted for food | *Something you play for fun with rules | One match in a sports competition
test: Each of the 12 groups played 6 games. How many games were played in total? | *72 | 66 | 62 | 18
exam: «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now.» What kind of games does Ruby stop? | *Video games | Wild games | Olympic Games | Board games
